    <string name="tv_require_pin_desc">New AirPlay devices must enter the 4-digit code shown on this TV. Apple TV Remote pairing always uses a code.</string>
    <string name="tv_color_range">Color Range</string>
    <string name="tv_color_range_desc">Black and white levels of the video output. Change it only if shadows look washed out or crushed; compare with the grayscale test.</string>
    <string name="tv_color_range_full">Full (0–255)</string>
    <string name="tv_color_range_limited">Limited (16–235)</string>
    <string name="tv_grayscale">Grayscale Test</string>
    <string name="tv_grayscale_desc">Near-black (0–32) and near-white (223–255) steps drawn by this TV, to compare with the same pattern cast over AirPlay and check for clipped levels. It is a local image and cannot prove that AirPlay video is uncompressed.</string>
    <string name="tv_grayscale_note">Drawn locally for comparison with a cast image. It does not prove AirPlay video is uncompressed. Press Back to exit.</string>
    <string name="tv_audio_delay">Audio Delay</string>
    <string name="tv_audio_delay_desc">Delay sound when it is out of sync with the picture. Off uses the default handling.</string>
    <string name="tv_audio_auto_buffer_desc">Tune the audio buffer to the network and this TV automatically. Fine tolerance is in Advanced.</string>
    <string name="tv_ms">%1$d ms</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_enable">Apple TV Remote</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_enable_desc">When on, the Apple TV Remote in iPhone Control Center can find and control this TV.</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_status">Status</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_status_desc">The first time you pair, this TV shows a 4-digit code to enter on iPhone.</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_access">Accessibility Service</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_access_desc">Some buttons need this app’s accessibility service. Press OK to open the system accessibility settings.</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_adb">Local Key Channel</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_adb_desc">Sends keys through this TV’s local ADB. Some buttons may not work while it is disconnected.</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_dpad">Directional Buttons</string>
    <string name="tv_remote_dpad_desc">The iPhone remote uses a swipe area by default. For directional buttons, turn on Directional Buttons in iPhone Settings › Accessibility › Apple TV Remote. That setting lives on iPhone; this app cannot change it.</string>
